licable to every verification story whose chokepoint is a package-level pure function (`pkg.Fn(args)` style): skip the shared-instance pattern entirely; the burst's value is the purity assertion on the package. (2) `DETERMINISTIC-ORDERING SELF-CHECK FIRES BEFORE THE TABLE WALK AND BEFORE THE BURST` — the coverage member's third head-of-test self-check calls `Diff(desired, actual)` TWICE on the same inputs for every scenario and reflect.DeepEquals the resulting plans. A regression that introduced map-iteration ordering into the plan emission (e.g. a hashmap walk instead of the existing `sort.Strings(unionKeys)`) would surface here as a fast targeted failure on the affected scenario row, NOT as a confusing per-iteration burst mismatch many lines later. Forward-applicable to every verification story whose chokepoint emits an ordered output from unordered inputs: pin determinism at the head of the test as its own self-check, separate from the per-row verdict; the property is structurally different from the closed-set tag and deserves its own seam. (3) `THE PER-ROW REDACTION CANARY IS GATED ON A row.seedValueMarker FLAG SO ONLY ROWS WHOSE MUTATOR ROUTES A VALUE THROUGH DesiredValue TRIGGER THE MARKER-SURVIVAL + MARKER-ABSENCE PREDICATE` — the value-free classification contract says env-var values reach Action ONLY via DesiredValue. The canary therefore seeds RECONCILESECRETMARKER ONLY in env-var-changed / env-var-missing scenarios (via the row's mutator, not a generic pre-mutator pass — important: a generic pass would bleed marker into the env-var-missing row's untouched baseline FOO value and produce an unwanted env_var_changed action, false-positiving the row's "missing" prediction). The predicate asserts (a) the marker survives in Action.DesiredValue of at least one update action, (b) the marker is absent from Action.Type / Kind / Reason / EnvVarKey, all ServiceRef ID fields, all DomainRef fields, AND all UnmanagedResource fields. Non-env-var rows (service_missing, do