st NOT strip it because it isn't a secret transport pattern), reject rows assert the marker never appears in `err.Error()`, `FieldViolation.Reason`, or `fmt.Sprintf("%+v", err)`. The head-of-test self-check probes `svc.redactor.Redact(marker)` and asserts the marker survives; without it, an over-aggressive redactor regression would silently false-positive every accept row's marker-survival assertion. Forward-applicable to every verification story whose chokepoint feeds a redactor and asserts marker-survival on accept paths — probe the redactor's pure projection of the marker before walking the table; the probe is the chokepoint between "redactor leaves benign data intact" and "marker-survival predicate is meaningful". (3) `REJECT-PATH REDACTION CANARY SCANS THREE SURFACES: err.Error(), apierr.ViolationsOf(err) FieldViolation.Reason, AND fmt.Sprintf("%+v", err)` — yerr.Error's serialised form may stash data in metadata fields the bare Error() string does not expose; scanning all three closes the gap so a future regression that started stashing the offending value in error metadata (NOT just the message) fails the redaction predicate too. Forward-applicable to every verification story whose typed error carries field-violation metadata — scan every operator-visible projection of the error for the marker, not just the bare message. Two store-layer gotchas worth pinning forward: (A) `NewBreakGlassService` requires non-nil store/orgs/sessions/audit even when the validator path never reaches them — the constructor's nil-guard is structural; the canonical-service helper passes `&Store{}` + `NewOrganizationRepository()` + `NewBreakGlassRepository()` + `nopAuditAppender{}` as placeholders the validator never reaches. (B) `breakGlassDefaultTTL` MUST be strictly less than `breakGlassMaxTTL` so non-capping accept rows can assert `ExpiresAt - StartedAt == TTL` exactly; the ttl_capped accept row sets TTL = breakGlassMaxTTL+time.Hour explicitly. Load-bearing invariant unchanged: ON