+  - `golangci-lint run ./...`
+  - `staticcheck ./...` attempted; `staticcheck` is not installed.
+  - `govulncheck ./...` attempted; `govulncheck` is not installed.
+- Results
+  - All required Go checks passed.
+  - `golangci-lint run ./...` passed with 0 issues after adding exported comments to the new job event API.
+- Remaining risks or follow-ups
+  - `goimports`, `staticcheck`, and `govulncheck` are unavailable in this environment.
+  - Future job-list/detail endpoints can expose `provisioning_job_events` alongside `job_attempts` when those API stories land.
+- **Learnings for future iterations:**
+  - `provisioning_jobs` now has two timelines: `provisioning_job_events` for every lifecycle transition and `job_attempts` for finished worker attempts only.
+  - Invalid provisioning-job lifecycle edges should use `apierr.InvalidStateTransition("provisioning_job", from, to)`, not generic `apierr.Conflict`.
+  - Transition callers may omit actor/request metadata; the repository derives a stable worker/system fallback from the lease/job row, but customer/admin paths should pass explicit actor metadata.
